<control>{"schema":"workflow-foreach-batch-v1","items":[{"id":"task-20","control":{"schema":"deep-research-verify-claim-v1","digest":"Verified server stderr logging permission.","id":"claim-007","status":"verified","confidence":"high","verdictDigest":{"support":"The cited primary specification explicitly permits UTF-8 stderr logging for informational, debug, and error messages.","sourceUrls":["https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/stdio.md"]},"evidence":[{"source":"Model Context Protocol specification — stdio","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/stdio.md","sourceRef":"wsrc_ff966eae34ec1ec6ab48a4f0cf055b83","quote":"The server **MAY** write UTF-8 strings to `stderr` for any logging purposes\n  including informational, debug, and error messages.","matchType":"exact","relevance":"Directly establishes permission, encoding, stream, and logging scope."}],"caveats":[],"correctionOrCounterclaim":""},"analysis":"An independent exact-source read confirms the claim verbatim. MAY permits logging; it does not require it. The UTF-8 statement here concerns stderr strings, not protocol-message encoding.","refs":[{"sourceRef":"wsrc_ff966eae34ec1ec6ab48a4f0cf055b83","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/stdio.md"}]},{"id":"task-21","control":{"schema":"deep-research-verify-claim-v1","digest":"Verified client stderr interpretation guidance.","id":"claim-008","status":"verified","confidence":"high","verdictDigest":{"support":"The cited primary specification explicitly says clients SHOULD NOT assume server stderr output indicates error conditions.","sourceUrls":["https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/stdio.md"]},"evidence":[{"source":"Model Context Protocol specification — stdio","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/stdio.md","sourceRef":"wsrc_ff966eae34ec1ec6ab48a4f0cf055b83","quote":"The client **MAY** capture, forward, or ignore the server's `stderr` output and\n  **SHOULD NOT** assume `stderr` output indicates error conditions.","matchType":"exact","relevance":"Directly states the claimed client-side normative guidance."}],"caveats":[],"correctionOrCounterclaim":""},"analysis":"An independent exact-source read confirms the claim verbatim, preserving SHOULD NOT rather than strengthening it to MUST NOT. This does not imply stderr can never contain actual errors.","refs":[{"sourceRef":"wsrc_ff966eae34ec1ec6ab48a4f0cf055b83","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/stdio.md"}]}]}</control>
